      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-3647",
      ":question/problem": "Calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x) = x\\sec x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We use the product rule, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xsec⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)\\cdot sec⁡x+x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(sec⁡x) \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot sec⁡x+x\\cdot (sec⁡xtan⁡x) \\\\  & =sec⁡x(1+xtan⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
    },
    ":knowledge-point/id": "9e4b3974-1288-524e-a34c-8091c0e072f1",
