        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1883",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y=\\frac{3}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{cos}x-3\\operatorname{sec}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We take the derivative of each term and then add them, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{-2}+\\operatorname{cos}x-3\\operatorname{sec}x) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{-3}+(-\\operatorname{sin}x)-3\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x \\\\  & =-6{x}^{-3}-\\operatorname{sin}x-3\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{{x}^{3}}-\\operatorname{sin}x-3\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
      {
        ":db/id": 17592186233611,
        ":question/difficulty": {
          ":db/ident": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
        },
        ":question/id": "bb909c2b-b4a1-545d-9302-d4f03a02a17d",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-1938",
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}x}{4x}.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}x}{4x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x)(4x)-(\\operatorname{sec}x)(4)}{(4x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4x\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x-4\\operatorname{sec}x}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(x\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x-\\operatorname{sec}x)}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sec}x\\operatorname{tan}x-\\operatorname{sec}x}{4{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
