        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ if $y=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}(x)}{5{x}^{2}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}(x)}{5{x}^{3}}($\n{{field-1}}$)$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,(\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}(x)}{5{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3\\operatorname{sec}(x)\\operatorname{tan}(x))(5{x}^{2})-(3\\operatorname{sec}(x))(10x)}{(5{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sec}(x)\\operatorname{tan}(x)-30x\\operatorname{sec}(x)}{25{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5x\\operatorname{sec}(x)(3x\\operatorname{tan}(x)-6)}{25{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}(x)(3x\\operatorname{tan}(x)-6)}{5{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\operatorname{sec}(x)}{5{x}^{3}}(x\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
