        ":question/worked-solution": "We calculate the derivative using the quotient rule, as follows:\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3sec⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3sec⁡xtan⁡x)({e}^{x})-(3sec⁡x)({e}^{x})}{({e}^{x})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{x}sec⁡x(tan⁡x-1)}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3sec⁡x(tan⁡x-1)}{{e}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
